  "decision_conditions": [
    "The first-floor side extension, by reason of bulk, mass,&nbsp;scale and design, would present a two-storey&nbsp;side extension with multiple&nbsp;separate roof forms and planes on the front elevation of the dwelling&nbsp;and unaligned fenestration which would create a disjointed and fragmented appearance unbalancing the uniformity&nbsp;of the terrace row. This would pose harm to the character of the dwelling and on the non-designated heritage&nbsp;asset.&nbsp;The proposal is therefore contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, December 2024)Policies D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2, DMD1, DMD4, DMD5 and Part 6 of SPP6 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)"
